WEBVTT

NOTE Episode: The Leaf They Didn't Touch

1
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:22.980
<v Old Timber>There is room on this dry stone, little ones, although Bongo has reserved half of it for a blueberry bowl.</v>

2
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:30.030
<v Old Timber>What happens when you say yes very quickly, then discover that keeping your yes is much harder than saying it?</v>

3
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:39.720
<v Old Timber>God cares whether our words can be trusted. That afternoon, three quick yeses were about to meet one very slow ten minutes.</v>

4
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:49.240
<v Old Timber>One warm afternoon, Fern the young fawn had been watching a water-lily flower beside one broad green leaf since breakfast.</v>

5
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:57.523
<v Old Timber>And three frogs who usually arrived with a question and left with four wrong answers wanted, for once, a serious job.</v>

6
00:00:58.223 --> 00:01:06.123
<v Old Timber>Shelly the young tortoise stood beside Fern's marker twig while Splish, Splash, and Splosh lined up on the bank.</v>

7
00:01:06.473 --> 00:01:13.625
<v Splish>We are ready for duty. Serious duty. My face is doing its least wiggly expression.</v>

8
00:01:13.975 --> 00:01:20.278
<v Splash>Mine is even less wiggly. I have moved all my wiggles into my left foot.</v>

9
00:01:20.628 --> 00:01:24.838
<v Splosh>I have no wiggles. I have rules.</v>

10
00:01:25.188 --> 00:01:28.026
<v Shelly>That is somehow more concerning.</v>

11
00:01:28.376 --> 00:01:38.036
<v Fern>I marked this leaf at breakfast. The flower beside it has been changing all day, and I need one final measure of how wide it stands open.</v>

12
00:01:38.386 --> 00:01:41.886
<v Splish>A final measure. That sounds very serious.</v>

13
00:01:42.236 --> 00:01:45.549
<v Splash>It sounds finaler than a normal measure.</v>

14
00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:47.719
<v Splosh>State the rules.</v>

15
00:01:48.069 --> 00:01:59.249
<v Shelly>For ten minutes, leave the marked leaf exactly as it is. Do not touch it, move it, blow it, splash it, or improve it.</v>

16
00:01:59.599 --> 00:02:00.918
<v Splish>Yes.</v>

17
00:02:01.268 --> 00:02:03.168
<v Splash>Yes yes.</v>

18
00:02:03.518 --> 00:02:08.384
<v Splosh>Official yes. Stamped, filed, and wearing a small hat.</v>

19
00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.706
<v Shelly>There is no hat.</v>

20
00:02:11.056 --> 00:02:13.105
<v Splosh>The hat is official.</v>

21
00:02:13.455 --> 00:02:21.675
<v Old Timber>Bongo the bear cub arrived with blueberries, and Zippy the hummingbird arrived with three timers for one ten-minute job.</v>

22
00:02:22.025 --> 00:02:27.677
<v Bongo>I brought guard snacks. I asked first, so the snacks are not helping without permission.</v>

23
00:02:28.027 --> 00:02:37.207
<v Zippy>Timer one counts minutes, timer two checks timer one, and timer three asks whether time feels watched.</v>

24
00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.942
<v Shelly>Time has declined to comment.</v>

25
00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:47.072
<v Fern>I will stay and write what the flower does. Shelly is fetching Professor Hoot's measuring reed.</v>

26
00:02:47.422 --> 00:02:51.802
<v Shelly>If anything changes, call me. I will be close enough to hear.</v>

27
00:02:52.152 --> 00:02:59.478
<v Fern>This is the first flower watch I planned and announced myself. I would like to finish it the way I began it.</v>

28
00:02:59.828 --> 00:03:06.448
<v Splash>You announced it? Out loud? Then this job is serious twice.</v>

29
00:03:06.798 --> 00:03:14.058
<v Shelly>Serious does not mean wearing a serious face. It means treating Fern's work as if it matters to you too.</v>

30
00:03:14.408 --> 00:03:20.448
<v Splosh>Then we will care for it with our faces, our rules, and all our feet.</v>

31
00:03:20.798 --> 00:03:23.818
<v Splish>It will not become hard. It is a leaf.</v>

32
00:03:24.168 --> 00:03:27.829
<v Splash>Leaves are famously easy not to touch.</v>

33
00:03:28.179 --> 00:03:30.799
<v Splosh>Begin Official Lily Watch.</v>

34
00:03:31.149 --> 00:03:38.329
<v Zippy>Ten minutes remaining. Also ten minutes have always been remaining. This is our first announcement.</v>

35
00:03:38.679 --> 00:03:45.059
<v Old Timber>Shelly had taken exactly four slow steps when the first blueberry escaped Bongo's bowl.</v>

36
00:03:45.409 --> 00:03:49.789
<v Bongo>That berry has left the bowl without permission.</v>

37
00:03:50.494 --> 00:03:57.594
<v Old Timber>The blueberry rolled toward the marked leaf, slow enough to be insulting and fast enough to require a decision.</v>

38
00:03:57.944 --> 00:04:01.524
<v Splish>I can blow it away. Breath has no hands.</v>

39
00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.654
<v Fern>Shelly said not to blow the leaf.</v>

40
00:04:05.004 --> 00:04:09.224
<v Splish>I would blow the berry. The leaf would merely experience nearby weather.</v>

41
00:04:09.574 --> 00:04:14.252
<v Splash>I can blow from the other side, so the weather cancels itself.</v>

42
00:04:14.602 --> 00:04:18.490
<v Splosh>Denied. Two weathers make climate.</v>

43
00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.019
<v Fern>Two breaths do not make climate.</v>

44
00:04:22.369 --> 00:04:25.549
<v Splash>Then they make a tiny weather argument.</v>

45
00:04:25.899 --> 00:04:30.439
<v Bongo>I can pick up my own berry if somebody tells me where to put my paws.</v>

46
00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:38.529
<v Fern>Left paw on the flat stone. Right paw behind the bowl. Reach from the bank, not over the water.</v>

47
00:04:38.879 --> 00:04:44.059
<v Bongo>Left, right, bank. I got this carefully.</v>

48
00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:54.310
<v Old Timber>Bongo reached. The berry rolled one berry-width farther. Bongo froze so completely that Zippy checked whether bears could pause.</v>

49
00:04:54.660 --> 00:05:00.800
<v Zippy>Confirmed. Bear paused. Nine minutes, twenty-seven seconds remain.</v>

50
00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.130
<v Splash>The berry is nearly touching our not-touching leaf.</v>

51
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:12.420
<v Splosh>Official ruling: berries are not frogs. The promise contains no berry clause.</v>

52
00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.875
<v Fern>The promise was to leave the leaf exactly as it is.</v>

53
00:05:17.225 --> 00:05:21.525
<v Splish>Exactly as it is, except possibly beside one blueberry.</v>

54
00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:28.975
<v Bongo>No. My snack should not become Fern's experiment. I am moving the whole bowl away.</v>

55
00:05:29.325 --> 00:05:36.905
<v Old Timber>On his second reach, Bongo caught the berry, but his elbow nudged the bowl and two more berries started rolling.</v>

56
00:05:37.255 --> 00:05:40.275
<v Bongo>I have created a berry meeting.</v>

57
00:05:40.625 --> 00:05:47.165
<v Fern>Hold the bowl against the flat stone first. Then gather the two rolling berries.</v>

58
00:05:47.515 --> 00:05:55.335
<v Old Timber>On his third attempt, Bongo steadied the bowl, caught both berries, and carried every snack beyond rolling distance.</v>

59
00:05:55.685 --> 00:06:01.745
<v Bongo>Guard snacks are now distant snacks. I will miss them with great care.</v>

60
00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:10.943
<v Zippy>Eight minutes, fifty-two seconds. No leaf contact. One berry incident. One excellent snack move.</v>

61
00:06:11.293 --> 00:06:14.553
<v Splosh>Official Lily Watch remains flawless.</v>

62
00:06:14.903 --> 00:06:18.213
<v Splish>Could we inspect the underside without touching the top?</v>

63
00:06:18.563 --> 00:06:19.823
<v Fern>No.</v>

64
00:06:20.173 --> 00:06:23.790
<v Splash>Could we inspect it from below while facing the top?</v>

65
00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.720
<v Fern>Still no.</v>

66
00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:30.610
<v Splosh>Excellent guarding. We have found two forbidden directions.</v>

67
00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.780
<v Splish>What about sideways?</v>

68
00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:35.570
<v Fern>The answer has stopped travelling.</v>

69
00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:43.922
<v Old Timber>For nearly a whole minute, they watched using only their eyes. It was the longest minute ever recorded by three frogs.</v>

70
00:06:44.272 --> 00:06:51.452
<v Zippy>Seven minutes, forty-one seconds remain. Your minute was truly nineteen seconds.</v>

71
00:06:51.802 --> 00:06:55.642
<v Splash>That explains why it felt slightly short for forever.</v>

72
00:06:55.992 --> 00:07:04.702
<v Zippy>You can count the leaf veins from here. Looking is allowed, counting is quiet, and neither one needs a tower.</v>

73
00:07:05.052 --> 00:07:06.630
<v Splish>I count eleven.</v>

74
00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:11.280
<v Splash>I count twenty-two because I counted each one louder.</v>

75
00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:16.490
<v Splosh>I count one leaf. I have won counting.</v>

76
00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:24.020
<v Fern>There are seventeen large veins on the side we can see. You stayed on the bank and learned something true.</v>

77
00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.590
<v Splish>That worked, which means we should immediately improve it with equipment.</v>

78
00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:33.399
<v Splish>I have a watching reed. A reed can look more closely than an eye.</v>

79
00:07:33.749 --> 00:07:36.289
<v Fern>A reed cannot look.</v>

80
00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:40.437
<v Splish>Then it has been holding the wrong end toward things for years.</v>

81
00:07:41.141 --> 00:07:51.621
<v Old Timber>Splish balanced the watching reed above the leaf. Splash held Splish steady. Splosh called it a tower and opened a meeting about touching.</v>

82
00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:57.547
<v Splosh>The reed is not a frog. Therefore the frog has not touched the leaf.</v>

83
00:07:57.897 --> 00:08:00.876
<v Fern>Does the leaf know who is holding the reed?</v>

84
00:08:01.226 --> 00:08:06.302
<v Splish>Leaves know less than reeds. This experiment is becoming worrying.</v>

85
00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:15.109
<v Splash>Closer. Just a little closer. Not touching is easier when you can see exactly what you are not touching.</v>

86
00:08:15.459 --> 00:08:23.249
<v Old Timber>The reed dipped. The leaf lifted. The marker twig moved one small twig-width across the water.</v>

87
00:08:23.599 --> 00:08:27.499
<v Splish>That was not a touch. That was a very short meeting.</v>

88
00:08:27.849 --> 00:08:29.669
<v Fern>My marker moved.</v>

89
00:08:30.019 --> 00:08:38.855
<v Zippy>Recording: reed touched leaf, leaf lifted, marker moved at six minutes and fifty-one seconds remaining.</v>

90
00:08:39.205 --> 00:08:45.051
<v Splosh>Record instead: leaf held an unasked meeting with reed.</v>

91
00:08:45.401 --> 00:08:52.421
<v Zippy>I only have a truth column. The other columns hold seconds, smaller seconds, and tiny fractions.</v>

92
00:08:52.771 --> 00:09:02.271
<v Bongo>I heard the marker move. Do you need me to bring Shelly back? I can go carefully and also quickly, in that order.</v>

93
00:09:02.621 --> 00:09:08.027
<v Splosh>Not yet. Official Lily Watch repairs its own official lilies.</v>

94
00:09:08.377 --> 00:09:14.837
<v Bongo>The lily is not official. But I will stay close enough to hear a different answer.</v>

95
00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:23.005
<v Fern>I need Shelly. I am saying that now, even if the brothers are not ready to say it with me.</v>

96
00:09:23.355 --> 00:09:29.553
<v Splash>We can move the marker back exactly. Then it will be as if the moving never moved.</v>

97
00:09:29.903 --> 00:09:31.831
<v Fern>But it did move.</v>

98
00:09:32.181 --> 00:09:34.961
<v Splish>Only in the first version of what happened.</v>

99
00:09:35.311 --> 00:09:38.512
<v Fern>There is only one version of what happened.</v>

100
00:09:38.862 --> 00:09:42.101
<v Splosh>Then it is fortunate we are still editing it.</v>

101
00:09:42.451 --> 00:09:48.351
<v Old Timber>The plain truth was waiting at the edge of the afternoon. The brothers were not ready to say it.</v>

102
00:09:48.701 --> 00:09:54.841
<v Splash>New plan. We move the water, not the marker. Water has no promise.</v>

103
00:09:55.191 --> 00:09:59.077
<v Splish>We make one tiny ripple from very far away.</v>

104
00:09:59.427 --> 00:10:03.407
<v Splosh>Approved, provided the ripple signs the visitor book.</v>

105
00:10:03.757 --> 00:10:10.418
<v Fern>Please stop. The measure is already changed. More moving will not make it unchanged.</v>

106
00:10:10.768 --> 00:10:16.028
<v Splosh>We are Official Lily Watch. We cannot finish with a moved marker.</v>

107
00:10:16.378 --> 00:10:19.798
<v Fern>You can finish by telling Shelly what happened.</v>

108
00:10:20.148 --> 00:10:23.488
<v Splish>Then we become Former Official Lily Watch.</v>

109
00:10:23.838 --> 00:10:32.097
<v Splash>And everybody will remember why serious jobs usually go to creatures with fewer songs about mud.</v>

110
00:10:32.447 --> 00:10:36.347
<v Splosh>We asked for one job that was not a joke.</v>

111
00:10:36.697 --> 00:10:42.517
<v Fern>I did not think your yes was a joke. I thought you would call Shelly when I asked.</v>

112
00:10:42.867 --> 00:10:50.677
<v Zippy>Five minutes, twelve seconds remain. I can call Shelly now, or I can keep counting while this gets harder.</v>

113
00:10:51.027 --> 00:10:52.687
<v Splosh>Keep counting.</v>

114
00:10:53.037 --> 00:10:54.762
<v Splash>Make the ripple.</v>

115
00:10:55.112 --> 00:11:02.692
<v Old Timber>Three frogs jumped at the far bank. Their ripple moved the leaf and tipped the reed tower into the shallows.</v>

116
00:11:03.042 --> 00:11:05.262
<v Splish>The ripple moved it more.</v>

117
00:11:05.612 --> 00:11:08.039
<v Splash>And the tower fell.</v>

118
00:11:08.389 --> 00:11:10.769
<v Splosh>Fern... we did that.</v>

119
00:11:11.119 --> 00:11:13.899
<v Fern>My flower measure is gone for today.</v>

120
00:11:14.601 --> 00:11:22.021
<v Old Timber>Nobody spoke for a breath. The flower kept closing, and no rule could make the afternoon begin again.</v>

121
00:11:22.371 --> 00:11:24.671
<v Splish>I moved the leaf with the reed.</v>

122
00:11:25.021 --> 00:11:29.181
<v Splash>I suggested the ripple after Fern asked us to stop.</v>

123
00:11:29.531 --> 00:11:34.151
<v Splosh>I cared more about keeping the title than keeping the promise.</v>

124
00:11:34.501 --> 00:11:40.561
<v Fern>Thank you for saying the true parts. What happens next must be true too.</v>

125
00:11:40.911 --> 00:11:50.651
<v Zippy>Four minutes, thirty-eight seconds remain. Shelly is still away. This is the last moment to tell her before she discovers it.</v>

126
00:11:51.001 --> 00:11:53.772
<v Splosh>Splash, you call loudest.</v>

127
00:11:54.122 --> 00:12:02.874
<v Splash>Shelly! Please come back now! Not in four minutes. We need the true version while it is still hard to say!</v>

128
00:12:03.224 --> 00:12:10.244
<v Bongo>I will find her. Fern, tell me first: do you need me to stay or go?</v>

129
00:12:10.594 --> 00:12:17.054
<v Fern>Go, please. Bring Shelly. I will keep the marker where it drifted.</v>

130
00:12:17.404 --> 00:12:26.264
<v Old Timber>Bongo took three careful steps and one very fast fourth. Shelly met him halfway, carrying Hoot's measuring reed.</v>

131
00:12:26.614 --> 00:12:29.474
<v Shelly>You called before the ten minutes ended.</v>

132
00:12:29.824 --> 00:12:36.364
<v Shelly>Did you call because I saw the moved marker, or because you chose to tell me before I could see it?</v>

133
00:12:36.714 --> 00:12:44.193
<v Splash>You had not seen it. That was the point. We wanted one true thing to happen before you arrived.</v>

134
00:12:44.543 --> 00:12:48.696
<v Splish>I touched the leaf with a reed after you said not to touch or move it.</v>

135
00:12:49.046 --> 00:12:53.026
<v Splash>I made us send a ripple after Fern said the measure was already changed.</v>

136
00:12:53.376 --> 00:13:00.602
<v Splosh>I tried to change Zippy's record because I wanted the Official Lily Watch title to stay ours.</v>

137
00:13:00.952 --> 00:13:12.052
<v Zippy>My record says berry, reed, moved marker, stop request, ripple, fallen tower, confession. In that order.</v>

138
00:13:12.402 --> 00:13:16.142
<v Shelly>Fern, what did their choices cost your work?</v>

139
00:13:16.492 --> 00:13:23.421
<v Fern>I cannot use today's final measure. I will need to mark another leaf tomorrow and watch again.</v>

140
00:13:23.771 --> 00:13:28.218
<v Splosh>Then Official Lily Watch is over. We give the title back.</v>

141
00:13:28.568 --> 00:13:32.845
<v Splish>We can take down every reed and put the marker beside Fern's notebook.</v>

142
00:13:33.195 --> 00:13:40.215
<v Splash>And tomorrow we can carry things, not guard the leaf. Our feet are less likely to get that job wrong.</v>

143
00:13:40.565 --> 00:13:49.425
<v Shelly>Start with the reeds. Bongo can restore the marker where Fern directs. Zippy keeps the record unchanged.</v>

144
00:13:49.775 --> 00:13:59.035
<v Old Timber>They worked before anyone explained the afternoon. Reeds came down. The twig returned. Fern chose tomorrow's place.</v>

145
00:13:59.385 --> 00:14:06.001
<v Splish>This reed touched the leaf. I am putting it with the record, not back where somebody could mistake it for innocent.</v>

146
00:14:06.351 --> 00:14:14.171
<v Splash>These were the ripple reeds. I am carrying them to the bank one at a time because a pile would become another idea.</v>

147
00:14:14.521 --> 00:14:23.701
<v Splosh>And this leaf badge says Official Lily Watch. I am placing it beside Fern's notebook. It does not belong on me today.</v>

148
00:14:24.051 --> 00:14:30.886
<v Fern>I will keep it with today's record, not throw it away. Tomorrow will show what you do next.</v>

149
00:14:31.236 --> 00:14:38.576
<v Bongo>Marker left one leaf-width, Fern? I am asking because my paws have opinions.</v>

150
00:14:38.926 --> 00:14:42.983
<v Fern>One leaf-width left. Thank you for asking.</v>

151
00:14:43.333 --> 00:14:51.142
<v Zippy>Two minutes, nine seconds remain. The first test is over. The honest record is complete.</v>

152
00:14:51.492 --> 00:14:55.071
<v Splish>I thought asking for help would make our yes smaller.</v>

153
00:14:55.421 --> 00:15:00.281
<v Splash>Not asking made the problem enormous. It had a tower.</v>

154
00:15:00.631 --> 00:15:06.931
<v Splosh>Tomorrow our yes will include four words: we will tell you.</v>

155
00:15:07.634 --> 00:15:15.774
<v Old Timber>The ten minutes ended without a bell, a tick, or another invention. Zippy simply lowered her smallest timer.</v>

156
00:15:16.124 --> 00:15:21.624
<v Zippy>Zero minutes remain. Time reports that it felt heavily watched.</v>

157
00:15:21.974 --> 00:15:26.754
<v Old Timber>Splosh, what did your yes need when keeping it became difficult?</v>

158
00:15:27.104 --> 00:15:31.404
<v Splosh>Truth sooner. Help sooner. Fewer rules.</v>

159
00:15:31.754 --> 00:15:36.294
<v Splish>A yes does not become honest because you explain around it very cleverly.</v>

160
00:15:36.644 --> 00:15:46.943
<v Splash>And saying this is hard is not the same as saying no. It might be how you keep your yes from becoming pretend.</v>

161
00:15:47.293 --> 00:15:49.993
<v Fern>Tomorrow, I can trust that sentence.</v>

162
00:15:50.343 --> 00:15:59.523
<v Bongo>My careful yes today was moving the berries. If I had dropped them again, I would have asked Fern where to step again.</v>

163
00:15:59.873 --> 00:16:06.225
<v Zippy>My yes was keeping the record unchanged, even when somebody asked for a wrong column.</v>

164
00:16:06.575 --> 00:16:13.994
<v Shelly>And my yes was returning when you called. Being trusted does not mean never needing another person.</v>

165
00:16:14.344 --> 00:16:23.197
<v Old Timber>Mm. They had found the meaning before I reached for the Bible. That is usually the best way for a story to arrive at a verse.</v>

166
00:16:23.547 --> 00:16:30.007
<v Old Timber>In the Bible, Matthew chapter five, verse thirty-seven records Jesus saying it plainly:</v>

167
00:16:30.357 --> 00:16:38.737
<v Old Timber>But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.</v>

168
00:16:39.087 --> 00:16:50.587
<v Shelly>Communication here means what we say. Jesus was teaching that our yes should be true and our no should be true without piling extra promises around them.</v>

169
00:16:50.937 --> 00:17:04.517
<v Shelly>The last phrase says extra promises and slippery explanations come from evil because they make room for hiding the truth. A plain answer needs no tower around it.</v>

170
00:17:04.867 --> 00:17:07.938
<v Splosh>That verse has excellent rules.</v>

171
00:17:08.288 --> 00:17:10.533
<v Splish>It has two rules.</v>

172
00:17:10.883 --> 00:17:14.195
<v Splash>That leaves lots of room for snacks.</v>

173
00:17:14.545 --> 00:17:23.645
<v Bongo>Distant snacks are ready again. I kept my yes to moving them, and now I am giving a careful yes to sharing.</v>

174
00:17:23.995 --> 00:17:32.748
<v Fern>Tomorrow's flower watch starts after breakfast. You may carry the notebook and tell me if your feet begin making plans.</v>

175
00:17:33.098 --> 00:17:37.078
<v Splosh>Our feet will submit all plans in writing.</v>

176
00:17:37.782 --> 00:17:44.482
<v Old Timber>Professor Hoot the owl arrived with his measuring reed and the expression of someone whose fact had been delayed.</v>

177
00:17:44.832 --> 00:17:53.804
<v Professor Hoot>Many water-lily flowers follow a daily opening-and-closing rhythm. Some open in morning light and begin closing later in the day.</v>

178
00:17:54.154 --> 00:17:58.580
<v Splash>So the flower keeps opening the same shop every morning?</v>

179
00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:06.830
<v Professor Hoot>For several flowering days, yes. Light and a plant signal called auxin help time the petals.</v>

180
00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:08.536
<v Splish>Ox in?</v>

181
00:18:08.886 --> 00:18:13.162
<v Professor Hoot>Auxin. A plant signal. No ox.</v>

182
00:18:13.512 --> 00:18:17.891
<v Splash>That is good. An ox would need a very wide leaf.</v>

183
00:18:18.241 --> 00:18:22.003
<v Professor Hoot>Closing is part of a rhythm the flower can repeat.</v>

184
00:18:22.353 --> 00:18:28.953
<v Fern>Then tomorrow is the next flower watch. The flower will do its part again.</v>

185
00:18:29.303 --> 00:18:37.960
<v Professor Hoot>Precisely. I had intended to say that with more syllables, but the fawn has supplied an efficient summary.</v>

186
00:18:38.662 --> 00:18:48.882
<v Old Timber>When your yes becomes hard, tell the truth early. If a promise feels unsafe, confusing, or too big, ask a trusted grown-up for help.</v>

187
00:18:49.232 --> 00:18:52.572
<v Splish>Also keep blueberries beyond rolling distance.</v>

188
00:18:52.922 --> 00:19:00.519
<v Old Timber>The brothers are filing tomorrow's foot plans now. There are seventeen pages. We may need a smaller yes.</v>

189
00:19:00.869 --> 00:19:04.529
<v Ranger Ray>See you next time, somewhere in Shiloh Creek.</v>
